#### Example 2: Schema Evolution - Adding Optional Field (v1.5.0 → v1.6.0)

**Before (v1.5.0):**
```json
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "ClaimSubmittedEvent",
  "version": "1.5.0",
  "fields": [
    {"name": "claimId", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "memberId", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "claimAmount", "type": "long"}
  ]
}
```

**After (v1.6.0) - Backward Compatible:**
```json
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "ClaimSubmittedEvent",
  "version": "1.6.0",
  "fields": [
    {"name": "claimId", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "memberId", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "claimAmount", "type": "long"},
    {
      "name": "priorAuthorizationId",
      "type": ["null", "string"],
      "default": null
    }
  ]
}
```

**Producer Code (Java) - Publishing with v1.6.0:**
```java
// Producer automatically uses latest schema version
ClaimSubmittedEvent event = ClaimSubmittedEvent.newBuilder()
    .setClaimId("CLM-2025-001234")
    .setMemberId("MBR-987654")
    .setClaimAmount(15050L)
    .setPriorAuthorizationId("PA-2025-5678")  // New field in v1.6.0
    .build();

kafkaProducer.send(new ProducerRecord<>("claims.submitted", event));
```

**Consumer Code (Java) - Reading with v1.5.0 (Backward Compatible):**
```java
// Consumer running v1.5.0 can still deserialize v1.6.0 messages
@KafkaListener(topics = "claims.submitted")
public void handleClaimSubmitted(ClaimSubmittedEvent event) {
    String claimId = event.getClaimId();        // ✅ Works
    String memberId = event.getMemberId();      // ✅ Works
    Long amount = event.getClaimAmount();       // ✅ Works
    // priorAuthorizationId field ignored (not present in v1.5.0 schema)
}
```

