#### Example 3: Breaking Change Migration (v2.5.0 → v3.0.0)

**Schema v2.5.0 (Old):**
```json
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "ProviderUpdatedEvent",
  "version": "2.5.0",
  "fields": [
    {"name": "providerId", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "legacyProviderId", "type": ["null", "string"], "default": null},
    {"name": "npi", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "name", "type": "string"}
  ]
}
```

**Schema v3.0.0 (New) - Breaking Change:**
```json
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "ProviderUpdatedEvent",
  "version": "3.0.0",
  "fields": [
    {"name": "providerId", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "npi", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "name", "type": "string"},
    {
      "name": "specialty",
      "type": {
        "type": "record",
        "name": "ProviderSpecialty",
        "fields": [
          {"name": "code", "type": "string"},
          {"name": "description", "type": "string"}
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Migration Code (Consumer):**
```java
// Before (v2.5.0)
public void handleProviderUpdated_v2(ProviderUpdatedEvent_v2 event) {
    String providerId = event.getLegacyProviderId();  // Old field
    String npi = event.getNpi();
    processProvider(providerId, npi);
}

// After (v3.0.0)
public void handleProviderUpdated_v3(ProviderUpdatedEvent_v3 event) {
    String npi = event.getNpi();  // Use NPI instead of legacy ID
    ProviderSpecialty specialty = event.getSpecialty();
    processProvider(npi, specialty.getCode());
}
```
